From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Swanson <rswanson05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:12:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: box each space and shade sidebar lines

Each space sits in a box; neighbouring spaces share a border row,
worktree children stay inside their parent's box, and each machine's
spaces are boxed under its name. Sidebars narrower than 12 columns go
without. Dragging a space below the last one marks the last box's
bottom edge.

Every other tab of a space, and every other waiting agent, is drawn a
few percent lighter than the terminal's reported background, and the
line under the mouse a step lighter still; the focused tab and space
keep their highlight. Hovering a tab line shows a card beside the
sidebar with the folder it works in and, for agents, the git branch.
Plain terminals show $ in the agent-number column and waiting agents
carry their tree number there.

Upstream's mouse_hits_use_stable_workspace_tab_and_pane_ids clicks the
row that is now a box border and fails by design.

